<problem><title>Video review questions</title>
<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />


<p>A dynamical system is described by the <ref to="doenet:7XUfXRgBFR5siU2z19gbxK"><term>autonomous differential equation</term></ref>:  

<md>  
  <mrow>\frac{dv}{dt} \amp= f(v)</mrow>
  <mrow>v(t_0) \amp=v_0 \;\;\text{(initial condition)}</mrow>
</md>
  where,
  <me>f(v) = <function variables="v" name="f">v^3-5v^2-8v+12</function>.</me>
</p>

<p>The function <m>f(v)</m> is graphed below.</p>  
 
<graph name="vWithf" size="large" aspectRatio="2" xmin="-3" xmax="8" ymin="-40" ymax="40" fixAxes="true">
  <xLabel><m>v</m></xLabel>
  <yLabel><m>f(v) = \frac{dv}{dt}</m></yLabel>
  <function styleNumber="5" extend="$f" />

</graph>


<p>Which of the statements below are true? (Select all that apply.)
  <answer selectMultiple="true">
    <choice><m>v(t)</m> is increasing  when <m>1 &lt; v &lt; 6</m></choice>
    <choice credit="1"><m>v(t)</m> is increasing when <m>v = -1</m></choice>
    <choice credit="1"><m>v(t)</m> is decreasing when <m>v = 5</m></choice>
    <choice><m>v(t)</m> is decreasing when <m>v > 6</m></choice>
  </answer>
</p>
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>For the dynamical system described above, we are now given the initial condition that <m>v(0) = 4</m>. Which of the following statements correctly describes the behavior of <m>v</m> as <m>t</m> increases?</p>
<answer>
  <choice><m>v</m> increases rapidly at first, then slows down as <m>t</m> increases, and approaches the value <m>v = 6</m>.</choice>
  <choice><m>v</m> decreases slowly at first, then begins to decrease more rapidly, approaching the value <m>v = 1</m>. </choice>
  <choice credit="1"><m>v</m> decreases rapidly at first, then begins to decrease more gradually, approaching the value <m>v = 1</m>. </choice>
</answer>
</exercise>  

</problem>
</section>

